      "node_id": "kg_doc_3",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Title: Apple Remote. The Apple Remote is a remote control device released in or after October 2005 by Apple Inc. for use with a number of its products which use infrared capabilities. The device was originally designed to interact with the Front Row media program on the iSight iMac G5 and is compatible with some later desktop and portable Macintosh computers. The first three generations of Apple TV used the Apple Remote as their primary control mechanism. It has now been replaced with the Siri Remote in the fourth generation. Prior to the Apple Remote, Apple produced several nameless IR remotes for products such as the Macintosh TV, TV tuner expansion boards, and the PowerCD drive.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999973655475,
      "temperature": 0.9999999973655475,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
